          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The notion of a
            %em lattice object
            is the generalization of that of
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lattice"} lattice
            as one passes from the ambient
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+sets"} category of sets
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internalization"} into
            more general ambient
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categories"} categories
            with suitable properties.
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            In a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finitely+complete+category"} finitely complete category
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %strong lattice object
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bicartesian+preordered+object"} bicartesian preordered object
            that is also a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/partially+ordered+object"} partially ordered object
